{
  "_README": [
    "Hand-authored model data. scripts/extract-plans.mjs turns the sources in",
    "assets-src/plans/ into images using the `pages` list below, and",
    "scripts/build-plans.mjs generates plans/index.html and plans/<slug>.html.",
    "",
    "Page roles come from each PDF's document outline ('The Poet-Foundation'),",
    "read by scripts/scaffold-plans.mjs. That outline is the one machine-readable",
    "label in these files that can be trusted. The printed sheet titles cannot:",
    "the brochures carry leftover hidden content layers that pdftoppm does not",
    "render but pdftotext still returns, so extracted text names the wrong sheet.",
    "the-maestro and the-visionary have no outline at all, so their page order was",
    "read off the rendered pages. So were all sixteen elevation captions, which are",
    "not in the outline either.",
    "",
    "`id` also names the output file: plans/img/<slug>-<id>.{webp,png,jpg}. The crop",
    "is measured per page - extract-plans.mjs keeps the tallest block of ink, which",
    "is always the drawing - so no band needs tuning. `band` [top, bottom] overrides",
    "that for one page; `crop: false` takes the page whole.",
    "",
    "A page can name an `image` under assets-src/ instead of coming from a brochure",
    "PDF. the-storyteller works that way: it is a house that has been built, so its",
    "'elevation' is the photograph from the home page.",
    "",
    "An elevation's `label` is the caption printed under the rendering. That caption",
    "is deliberately cropped OUT of the image (Leavitt asked for it off the site),",
    "so the label survives only as the image's alt text.",
    "",
    "Models are listed in the order they appear at /plans/: alphabetical by the",
    "name after 'The'.",
    "",
    "SPECS COME FROM LEAVITT'S OWN FIGURES AND NOTHING HERE MAY BE GUESSED.",
    "",
    "`sqft` is living square footage. `sqftFrom` true means their sheet said",
    "'starting at', rendered as 'From 2,626'; false means the figure is exact.",
    "`price` is the starting price and `priceFrom` marks it the same way. Leavitt's",
    "note on that sheet - 'starting at means without additional options' - is not",
    "decoration: build-plans.mjs prints it alongside every price on the site, and it",
    "must keep travelling with them.",
    "",
    "`sqftNote`, `bathsNote` and `priceNote` print a qualifying line under a figure,",
    "for the cases one number cannot carry honestly: the-storyteller gains 70 sq ft",
    "with the three-car garage, and its bath count has an optional basement full",
    "bath on top.",
    "",
    "`stories` is observable from the plan set - no second-floor sheet means a",
    "single-story house. A missing value renders 'On request'; it is never filled",
    "in with a guess.",
    "",
    "`pricesAsOf` dates the whole price list, and is printed with the prices."
  ],
